/-!
# The original PSL₂(4) containment and five-point marking

The actual Borel has its full A₄ star image and cubic two-core quotient.
Two-perfectness makes it generated by cubics, so the original overlap theta
identity places it in L₁. In the ordinary local case its three-part forces
L₁≤K. In the covered case, noncontainment produces the two marked central
factors: L₀ contradicts the original normalizer bound; L₁,+ makes the same
prescribed outer inverter inner. This proves containment without the legacy
Borel residual/index identities.

Containment forces the ordinary A₆ local quotient, since the covered
order-nine quotient cannot embed through the two-core into A₅. Source
seed generation gives H=KT and U_H=[U_H,K]. The outer action identifies
H* with S₅, retaining K* as its actual A₅ subgroup. The original Borel and
overlap then construct equivariant five-point coordinates for H*/(H∩M)*,
the precise permutation carrier consumed by 13.8.4(5).

The terminal permutation contradiction and original 13.8.19–21 assembly
remain with qt-d-138-fields-source. Earlier source premises retain their
producers through qt-d-1381-source.
Source: Aschbacher–Smith, 13.8.20(b), printed p.955, using 13.7.3(9),
13.2.2(9) and the actual Borel on pp.954–955.
-/

